-- title:
--   Finite generation from homogeneous coordinate-power relations
-- statement:
--   For positive rational weights and homogeneous generators of one common positive degree, coordinate powers in their ideal imply that the polynomial ring is finite as a module over the algebra generated by those polynomials.
-- source:
--   openai/math Ampleness stack: WeightedIdealCurveBound implies eps-ample exceptional twist, hence Serre vanishing and eventual generation of I^n by weight ≤ n(rho+eps) sections.

